// NO UNIT TESTS REQUIRED FOR article.model.ts
// 
// Rationale:
// - article.model.ts contains only TypeScript interface definitions (compile-time type checking)
// - No runtime logic, branches, or conditionals exist in this file
// - The optional readingTime field is a pure type annotation with no executable code
//
// Test Coverage Strategy:
// The readingTime feature is comprehensively tested at the appropriate layers:
//
// 1. Unit Tests (article.mapper.ts):
//    - Test calculateReadingTime() helper function with various word counts
//    - Verify Math.ceil(wordCount / 200) calculation logic
//    - Test edge cases: null/undefined body, empty string, very short content
//    - Ensure minimum value of 1 minute is enforced
//
// 2. Integration Tests (article.service.test.ts - already specified in Tier 4):
//    - Verify readingTime field presence in getArticle() responses
//    - Verify readingTime field presence in getArticles() list responses
//    - Verify readingTime field presence in getFeed() responses
//    - Test with articles of varying body lengths (50, 200, 450 words)
//    - Validate readingTime values match expected calculations
//
// 3. Type Safety:
//    - TypeScript compiler validates the Article interface at build time
//    - Optional field (readingTime?: number) ensures backward compatibility
//    - Any code consuming Article type will get compile-time type checking
//
// Recommendation:
// Focus test efforts on article.mapper.ts (calculation logic) and 
// article.service.test.ts (integration testing) as outlined in the 
// execution tiers. No additional tests needed for this model file.
